From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:07:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-atari

Atari 2600 and Atari 7800 get one shelf each, Games/A2600 (.a26, .bin)
and Games/A7800 (.a78), on Stella 2014 (stella2014) and ProSystem
(prosystem) alone. Platform::A2600 and Platform::A7800 are appended to
SHELVES and Core::Stella2014 and Core::Prosystem to EVERY; upstream's ALL
lists stay as they are. The shelves are keyed by folder, so a 2600 .bin
never meets the Mega Drive or 32X .bin. Every policy method answers both
systems explicitly: slot keeps L1, R1, L2 and R2, X and Y pass to the
game, no core picker, no crop, rewind on.

The cores draw into their own canvases, 360x256 for Stella (up to 256
rows) and 360x272 for ProSystem (272 PAL rows), so no frame is halved.
Each system has its own Screen section, shown only when the card holds
its games: Shader (the retro list, Config/a2600_shader.txt and
a7800_shader.txt), Picture (4:3 by default, Stretch, Actual), PAL Speed
(Native by default, ADR 0071), Left and Right Difficulty, and TV Type on
the 2600 or BIOS on the 7800, kept in Config/atari.txt.

The console switches are RetroPad buttons in both cores. slot holds the
chosen switch button every frame (Stella latches, ProSystem reads it
only while held): 2600 L or L2, R or R2, L3 or R3, nothing on Auto, so
the game's own default stands; 7800 L and R held for B, ProSystem's own
defaults (left B, right A) as the factory choice. Both face buttons fire
on the 2600, and fire Stella's paddle button too; the left stick reaches
Stella's paddles. 7800 B and A are buttons 1 and 2, X is Reset, SELECT
Select and START Pause. With BIOS Off, ProSystem is opened with an empty
system dir (Saves/A7800/.system) so a 7800 BIOS in BIOS/ is never used.
The shelf shows the Master System cart until the Atari carts land.
